repository-code: 'https://github.com/Sukhmangill977/gc-ir-reference'
url: 'https://github.com/Sukhmangill977/gc-ir-reference'
date-released: '2026-09-09'
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and empirical artifact for a deterministic method that
  compiles approved AI governance assessments into enforceable runtime predicates.
  Implements the governed semantic refinement relation Psi_K closed by a signed
  judgment record, the GC-IR record family with total risk disposition, the
  deterministic compiler Phi with RFC 8785 canonicalization and SHA-256 bundle
  hashing, authority closure against an approved action matrix, the consequence-class
  gate coverage rule, a separately signed lifecycle registry, and a temporally valid
  traceability model with six audit queries. Ships two hash-pinned worked cases, an
  adversarial corpus, property-based tests, and a preregistered evaluation campaign.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - risk register
  - policy compilation
  - semantic refinement
  - runtime enforcement
  - agentic AI
  - model risk management
  - non-compensatory aggregation
  - traceability
  - RFC 8785
  - JSON canonicalization
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      From Risk Register to Runtime Predicate: A Deterministic Method for
      Compiling AI Governance Assessments into Enforceable Controls
